- RFC author given names are expanded from memory (the RFCs and Crossref print initials only: "B. Laurie", "A. Backman", and so on). If you want only what was confirmed, replace given names with initials. RFC 9943 first names likewise.
- `rfc9421`: BibTeX cannot mark two of three authors as editors; the RFC front page reads "A. Backman, Ed.; J. Richer, Ed.; M. Sporny".
